-- title:
--   The Gauss correction character Λ of OpenAI's Primitive roots paper is a Hecke character of angular type ±1 — Λ((α)) = ∏_w (w(α)/|w(α)|)^{m_w} for α ≡ 1 mod 𝔪^j
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the $n$-th roots of unity, with $n > 0$ and $12 \mid n$ (`IsCyclotomicExtension {n} ℚ F`), and let $\iota : F \to \mathbb C$ be a ring homomorphism. There is $N_0$ such that for every nonzero ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $\mathcal O_F$ divisible by every nonzero prime ideal of norm at most $N_0$ (`SmallPrimesDvd N₀ 𝔪`) there are $j \ge 0$ and $m : W \to \mathbb Z$ ($W$ the infinite places) with $m(w) = \pm1$ for every $w$, such that for every nonzero $\alpha \in \mathcal O_F$ with $\alpha - 1 \in \mathfrak m^j$,
--   $$\Lambda(\alpha\mathcal O_F) = \prod_{w \in W} e^{i\,m(w)\arg(w.\mathrm{embedding}\,\alpha)},$$
--   where $\Lambda$ = `gaussLambda ι` is the completely multiplicative function on ideals with $\Lambda(\mathfrak p) = -(\mathrm N\mathfrak p)^{-1/2} J(\rho_{\mathfrak p}, \rho_{\mathfrak p})$ at primes.
--
--   This is a cut for `exists_cutoff_exists_sChar_sEmb_gen_eq_thetaChar_mul_residueSymbol`, used with `exists_cutoff_prod_gaussPhase_three_span_eq_one`; that reduction is proved in Lean.
--
--   In the paper this is the part of Lemma 3.4 (p. 13) about $\Lambda$: the Jacobi sum evaluation (3.12) (p. 14), the Davenport–Hasse lifting formula, and $\Lambda = \Lambda_{E_0} \circ \mathrm N_{F/E_0}$ with $E_0 = \mathbb Q(\omega)$.
--
--   OpenAI, *Primitive roots for every admissible integer base* (2026), p. 14: “On a principal ideal generated by $a \equiv 1 \pmod 3$ its value is $a/|a|$; thus it is the unitary Hecke character of finite conductor dividing (3) and angular infinity type of exponent 1, in ideal-character convention. Set $\Lambda = \Lambda_{E_0} \circ \mathrm N_{F/E_0}$. […] The local norm at infinity is a product of complex coordinates or their conjugates. Consequently its angular exponent at each complex place of $F$ is 1 or −1, with no radial factor. Pullback by norm is unramified wherever $\Lambda_{E_0}$ is unramified, so its finite conductor is supported in $S$.”
--
--   **Formalization note.** "Hecke character with conductor supported in $S$ and angular type $m$" is stated through its values on principal ideals $(\alpha)$, $\alpha \equiv 1 \pmod{\mathfrak m^j}$.
-- source:
--   OpenAI, Primitive roots for every admissible integer base, OpenAI Math Release preprint, October 4, 2026, https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Primitive-roots-for-every-admissible-integer-base-October-4-2026/primitive-roots-all-integer-bases.pdf (Apache-2.0), p. 13–14, Lemma 3.4, the character Λ: (3.12), the Davenport–Hasse lifting formula and Λ = Λ_{E₀} ∘ N_{F/E₀} (Λ is a Hecke character with conductor in S and angular type ±1); a cut for exists_cutoff_exists_sChar_sEmb_gen_eq_thetaChar_mul_residueSymbol

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_ArtinHecke
import Definitions.Def_ArtinHeckeProbe
import Definitions.Def_ArtinHeckeTheta

namespace ArtinPrimitiveRoots

open NumberField UniqueFactorizationMonoid

theorem exists_cutoff_exists_gaussLambda_span_eq_prod_toCircle (n : ℕ) (hn0 : 0 < n) (hn : 12 ∣ n)
    (F : Type*) [Field F] [NumberField F] [IsCyclotomicExtension {n} ℚ F] (ι : F →+* ℂ) :
  ∃ N₀ : ℕ, ∀ 𝔪 : Ideal (𝓞 F), 𝔪 ≠ ⊥ → SmallPrimesDvd N₀ 𝔪 →
    ∃ (j : ℕ) (m : InfinitePlace F → ℤ), (∀ w, m w = 1 ∨ m w = -1) ∧
      ∀ α : 𝓞 F, α ≠ 0 → α - 1 ∈ 𝔪 ^ j →
        gaussLambda ι (Ideal.span {α}) =
          ∏ w, ((AddCircle.toCircle (m w • ((Complex.arg (w.embedding (α : F)) : ℝ) :
            AddCircle (2 * Real.pi))) : Circle) : ℂ)
  := by
  sorry

end ArtinPrimitiveRoots
